                <pb facs="1106" n="1006" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg1006"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 388.—Translation from the “Phare
                        d’ Alexandrie,” April 6, 1880.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">news of the day</hi>.</head>
                <p>We publish here below the decree appointing the members of the commission of
                    liquidation instituted by the decree of March 31.</p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">decree.</hi></p>
                <p>We, Khedive of Egypt:</p>
                <p>Considering Our decree of the 31st of March, 1880, instituting a commission of
                    liquidation:</p>
                <p>We decree—</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article</hi> 1. The following are appointed members
                    of the commission of liquidation: Sir Rivers Wilson, president, Messrs.
                    Baravelli, Bellaigue de Bughas, Colvin, De Kremer, Liron d’Airoles, De
                    Treskow.</p>
                <p>The government delegates Boutros Bey Ghali to represent it before the
                    commission.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Art</hi>. 2. The deliberations of the commission of
                    liquidation shall be taken by a majority of votes.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">Done at the palace of Abdin, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1880-03-05">this 5th day of April, 1880 (25th
                            Rabi-el-Akher, 1297.)</date></dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>MEHEMET TEWFIK.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>By the Khedive:</p>
                    <p>The President of the Council of Ministers:<lb/><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Riaz</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>


